# Shell scripts MUST stay LF, even on Windows.
#
# This repo is developed on Windows with `core.autocrlf=true`, which rewrites LF to CRLF on
# checkout. For a shell script that is fatal and non-obvious: the shebang becomes
# `#!/usr/bin/env bash\r`, and bash reports `bad interpreter: ... ^M` — or, worse, a `\r`
# lands mid-script and produces a syntax error pointing at the wrong line.
#
# The session that added `scripts/docs-lint.sh` did not hit this, because its own working
# copy was written with LF and never re-checked-out. A fresh clone would have. Added
# 2026-07-27, when `git add` warned "LF will be replaced by CRLF" on the new scripts.
*.sh text eol=lf
